  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Tocainide and Scn4a, mediated through the voltage-gated sodium channel complex. Tocainide is reported to bind to Scn7a, which is part of the voltage-gated sodium channel complex and is participated by Scn4a. This indicates that Tocainide may interact with Scn4a through a shared pathway involving Scn7a. Additionally, Tocainide is also reported to bind to Scn10a, which similarly participates in the voltage-gated sodium channel complex and is also participated by Scn4a. The evidence suggests that Tocainide may influence Scn4a through a common intermediary, Scn7a or Scn10a, which are both involved in the same functional complex. The scores from the paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, with varying degrees of support from different pathways. The integration of these findings suggests that Tocainide may exert its effects on Scn4a through a mechanism involving the voltage-gated sodium channel complex, though further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct interaction.",
